n=A.p(["CORE",A.b(["The income statement measures performance over a period; the balance sheet shows assets, liabilities and equity at a date; the cash-flow statement explains operating, investing and financing cash movements. Accrual profit is not the same as cash. Tie statements to the trial balance, subledgers, bank evidence and close schedules. Worked case: \u20b912 lakh profit with only \u20b91 lakh bank cash requires a profit-to-cash bridge covering receivables, inventory, supplier payments, capital expenditure and debt movements.","Working capital = current assets \u2212 current liabilities. The cash conversion cycle is DIO + DSO \u2212 DPO. If DIO=42 days, DSO=38 and DPO=30, CCC=50 days. Use consistent periods and definitions. Improving collections can release cash, but do not optimise DPO by violating supplier terms or damaging supply continuity.","Preventive controls stop errors, detective controls identify them and corrective controls resolve them. Reconciliation compares independent records, explains differences and assigns owners. If AP subledger is \u20b99.8 crore and GL is \u20b910 crore, do not post a plug: investigate timing, interface failures, journals, cut-off and mapping. Segregation of duties prevents one person completing incompatible steps unchecked."],q),"OPS",A.b(["P2P flow: requisition \u2192 PO \u2192 receipt \u2192 invoice capture \u2192 matching \u2192 approval \u2192 payment \u2192 bank/GL reconciliation. Two-way match compares invoice to PO; three-way match also checks receipt. An invoice above PO/receipt tolerance remains blocked until Procurement/Receiving evidence resolves it. Never split or force it through to meet a KPI.","O2C covers order, credit check, fulfilment, billing, AR, collections, cash application and dispute resolution. Overdue balances may be caused by billing errors, delivery disputes, credit risk or unapplied cash. Match receipts only with bank/remittance evidence. Segment collection work by value, age, reason, risk and owner.","Month-end close sequences cut-off, subledger completion, accruals/prepayments, reconciliations, review and reporting. An accrual recognises an expense incurred but not yet invoiced; a prepayment allocates a payment to future periods. A suspense balance is temporary and must have an owner, evidence, target date and escalation\u2014not become a permanent parking place."],q),"DATA",A.b(["Define the data grain and report date before using Excel. Validate dates, blanks, duplicate keys, statuses and totals. SUMIFS adds values meeting multiple criteria; COUNTIFS counts matching records; IF/AND can flag an invoice overdue only when it is unpaid and due before the report date. Reconcile calculated value to source before publishing.","Power Query records repeatable import and cleaning steps. Append stacks compatible tables; merge joins tables by keys. Standardise headers/types, trim text and map supplier IDs. Do not remove repeated supplier names blindly because a supplier can legitimately have many invoices. Keep unmapped rows in an exception query and reconcile counts and amounts after refresh.","A dashboard should support a decision. Define KPI numerator, denominator, period, filters, source, owner and refresh cadence. In a star schema, a fact table stores events/measures at a defined grain and dimension tables describe date, supplier, entity or reason. DAX measures respond to filter context. Validate relationships and totals against source records."],q),"AI",A.b(["Map and measure a process before automating it. RPA suits stable UI tasks; workflow routes approvals; APIs connect systems; OCR/IDP extracts fields; AI may classify or flag anomalies. Redesign unstable processes and poor master data first. Include build, support, monitoring and exception costs. Net annual benefit = measurable benefit \u2212 annual run/support cost.","OCR turns image text into machine-readable text; IDP adds document classification and field extraction. Extraction is not validation: check supplier, invoice ID, date, currency, arithmetic, duplicate risk, PO/receipt and approval. Low-confidence or conflicting fields go to a reviewer with source image and audit trail. Track false accepts separately from false rejects.","Human-in-the-loop AI requires an authorised reviewer with context, training and power to override. An anomaly flag is not proof of fraud. Define risk tiers, thresholds, permitted use, prohibited decisions, privacy, logs, escalation and monitoring. Never place confidential finance or personal data in an unapproved public tool."],q),"TECH",A.b(["Payment journey can include initiation, authentication, authorisation, processing, clearing, settlement, posting and reconciliation. \u201cAccepted\u201d is not proof of settlement. Trace transaction IDs, timestamps and independent processor/bank records. Handle pending, rejected, returned and reversed states separately; blind retries can create duplicate payments.","An API defines system requests and responses. A timeout does not prove the operation failed. Idempotency keys help repeated requests avoid duplicate effects. Validate inputs, authenticate callers, use least privilege, bounded retries and correlation IDs; then reconcile sent, accepted, rejected and settled transactions.","Fintech threats include phishing, credential theft, account takeover, payment redirection, API abuse and insider misuse. Use least privilege, MFA, independent bank-detail verification, maker-checker approvals, logs and timely access removal. Verify sensitive changes through a previously trusted channel, not the contact details in the change request."],q),"CHANGE",A.b(["Start with a defined problem and baseline. Map steps, queues, handoffs, rework and controls; distinguish symptoms from root causes and validate causes with samples/data. Example: if 45% of overdue invoice blocks are missing receipts, work with Receiving before proposing generic reminders or automation.","A user story states user, capability and value. Acceptance criteria are observable pass/fail conditions covering business rules, edge cases, data quality, access, reconciliation and error handling. Example: every in-scope invoice appears once, totals reconcile to source, unmapped reasons remain visible and access is role-based. Agile does not mean no documentation or no controls.","A deployed dashboard is an output; reduced overdue value without increased control failures is an outcome. A benefit needs a baseline, target, calculation, source, owner and assumptions. Released capacity is not automatically cash savings. Plan milestones, dependencies, risks, training, feedback and post-launch benefit reviews."],q),"EXCEL",A.b(["Workbook architecture: separate raw data, transformation, calculation, checks and presentation. Use Excel Tables, explicit report dates, consistent types and controlled inputs. Build a source-to-report reconciliation before interpreting results.","Formula foundations: relative, absolute and mixed references; IF, AND, OR, IFERROR, SUMIFS, COUNTIFS, date functions and structured references. Test blanks, invalid dates, negative amounts and boundary conditions instead of hiding errors indiscriminately.","Lookup and array analysis: use XLOOKUP or INDEX/MATCH with exact-match logic; define duplicate-key handling and missing-match outcomes. Dynamic arrays can simplify unique lists and filtering, but users must understand spill behaviour and version compatibility.","Power Query pipeline: import, type, trim, clean, merge, append, group and refresh using repeatable steps. Validate row counts and control totals; handle schema changes and rejected rows transparently.","Reporting capstone: turn a reconciled AP dataset into a decision-ready ageing pack with KPI definitions, filters, exception owners, refresh controls, assumptions and a documented reviewer sign-off."],q)],s,o)
